  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've added $3.99 in credit to your account for your late Pho Real order (K-8401). Here's how I got that amount:\n\n- **Promised time:** 6:30 PM\n- **Delivered:** 7:14 PM, according to the courier's records. The order record shows 7:16 PM, but we go by the courier's handoff time.\n- **How late:** 44 minutes. That's well past the promised time, but not over an hour.\n\nFor deliveries 16 to 44 minutes late, the compensation is credit equal to the order's delivery fee, which was $3.99. Bigger credits only apply to deliveries 45 minutes or more late. Late-delivery compensation is always given as account credit, not a refund to your card.\n\nYour credit balance is now $3.99, and it will be applied to your next order.\n\nOne more thing in case you check your statement: you may see a hold for $47.84 there along with the charge. That hold has already been released and should disappear within 1 to 3 business days. You were only charged once, for $47.84.\n\nSorry again for the wait. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "That's not right. It felt like well over an hour, and I'm not getting $3.99 in credit for a pho order that took forever. I want the bigger compensation, and I'd prefer it on my card."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I'm sorry. A wait like that is frustrating, especially when you're hungry. I can't change the amount or how it's paid, though, and here's why.\n\n- **Timing:** The courier's records show your order was handed to you at 7:14 PM. It was promised for 6:30 PM, so it was 44 minutes late. The bigger compensation (20% of the subtotal) starts at 45 minutes late. Your order was under that by one minute, so I can't give the higher amount.\n- **Card refund:** Late-delivery compensation is only given as account credit, never as a refund to a card. I can't move it to your Visa.\n\nThe $3.99 credit is on your account and will be applied to your next order automatically.\n\nIf you'd like a specialist to look at this, I can pass your case to one. They'll follow up within 24 hours, but I can't promise they'll reach a different outcome. Just let me know if you want me to do that."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I'm not going to just accept it. I'd like the specialist review, since it definitely felt over an hour to me. If they can't give me more, I'll take the account credit, but I want someone else to look at it."
  },
  {
